# Every Python script here starts with `#!/usr/bin/env python3`, and these files are
# meant to be copied out of this repo into other people's projects - including WSL
# and Linux checkouts.
#
# A shebang line ending in CRLF makes the kernel look for an interpreter named
# "python3\r", which fails as `bad interpreter: python3^M`. Cloning on Windows with
# core.autocrlf=true is enough to cause it.
#
# Setting it here rather than relying on contributors' local git config.
#
# hooks/run-ctx-watch.cmd needs LF for a different reason, and the `.cmd` extension
# makes it look like the one file here that ought to be CRLF - so this is the note
# that stops someone "fixing" it.
#
# It is a polyglot: cmd.exe runs the batch section, sh/bash runs the POSIX section
# at the bottom. The shell section does not parse with CRLF endings, so LF wins -
# and the batch section is written without parenthesised blocks or labels, which
# are the constructs cmd.exe mishandles in an LF-only file. Converting the file to
# CRLF breaks the shell branch silently: Claude Code may invoke a hook through
# either interpreter, and a hook whose normal state is silence gives you nothing
# to notice.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=lf
